diff --git a/docs/architecture/j2k-reset.md b/docs/architecture/j2k-reset.md
index fe62ea3ca7d8e9b5133619bfc20a7805b486e77e..3a2f271600a8d61865e16cf88727cdbeaf7a861c 100644
--- a/docs/architecture/j2k-reset.md
+++ b/docs/architecture/j2k-reset.md
@@ -84,6 +84,8 @@ Built-in source settings are another deliberate adapter seam. `BrowseSourceContr
 
 Saved source searches are an approved filter-sheet seam. One action on J2K's existing `SourceFilterSheet` stores the current query and recursively typed filter values through `SavedSourceSearchStore`. Restoring starts from the source's current filter schema and applies only structurally compatible values, so an extension update cannot replay an invalid select or sort index. The data is a bounded Hayai preference and therefore travels through J2K's existing preference backup rather than a second backup pipeline.
 
+The October metadata repair adds `NovelSeriesType` to the existing J2K genre-based type contract. `Manga.kt` delegates novel-tag recognition and its localized type label to Hayai; the existing details and bulk library editors use the shared series-type array. No type column, settings model, or library is added. The details/library presenters remove conflicting series tags before saving `Novel` through J2K's custom metadata. `NovelContentIdentity` classifies explicit novel tags before source or retained side-data evidence. The sole reader adapter and J2K download queue use that same identity, allowing an older text entry to be corrected even when its source lacks the current novel marker. The source must still provide real text or a saved document; changing a label cannot manufacture chapter content. J2K's existing custom-info backup option preserves this choice.
+
 The `ExtensionInstaller.kt` and `ExtensionInstallerJob.kt` seams retain J2K's package installation and WorkManager scheduling. They make a package operation cancellable while queued, downloading, or installing, reject missing downloads/sessions as terminal retry states, and subscribe before producing installation events. Hayai owns small operation policies and batch cancellation. Existing extension manager/UI adapters publish newly installed untrusted APKs to the trust UI and cancel by package identity. `ShizukuInstaller` exposes cancellation of only the requested waiting package; cancellation is unavailable after its privileged session has committed. These seams do not introduce another installer or extension catalog.
 
 Tsundoku extensions can implement its compile-only `eu.kanade.tachiyomi.source.SourceTracker` and `RateLimited` contracts. The compatibility declarations live under Hayai's `novel/compat` directory, with the required upstream package name as an explicit binary-interface exception. Preserve their interfaces, signatures, and Kotlin default implementations during minification. WTR-LAB and Novel Phoenix at NovelSourcery source commit `432f591ceac7a7bdd2d8ae9e65fa4ec91744320b` require these interfaces. This prevents class resolution failures; source-owned tracking callbacks remain **Foundation** and are not a claimed tracking port. Production callback dispatch remains separately audited, and no parallel rate-limit settings or chapter queue is added.
